### Command execution span

Status: [[image: Development]](https://camo.githubusercontent.com/51c52913babf0af7e3699435eb2fa53f65cf91d89c23a9e0edba0fdd9de155d0/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f2d646576656c6f706d656e742d626c7565)

Describes a tool call that executes one or more commands.

This refinement applies when a tool represents command execution, including the execution of skill's script.

Examples include:

- [OpenAI Agents](https://openai.github.io/openai-agents-python/sandbox/guide/) exec_command, which runs both general commands and scripts from materialized skills;
- [LangChain Deep Agents](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/deepagents/overview)sandbox execute, which runs both general commands and skill scripts;
- [Strands Agents](https://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/sdk/plugins/skills/) shell, which is used for both general commands and bundled skill scripts;
- [Anthropic](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/bash-tool)client bashfor general commands;
- [Google ADK](https://adk.dev/skills/) run_skill_script, which is dedicated to scripts bundled with skills;
- [Agno](https://docs.agno.com/skills/overview) get_skill_scriptwhen called with execute=true.

Instrumentations MAY also emit additional spans following the [CLI client span conventions](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/semconv/cli/cli-spans/)for each observed command, script, or process execution.

Span nameSHOULD be:

- execute_tool {gen_ai.tool.name} {gen_ai.skill.name} {gen_ai.skill.resource.name}when the skill and resource names are both available;
- execute_tool {gen_ai.tool.name} {gen_ai.skill.resource.name}when only the skill resource name is available;
- execute_tool {gen_ai.tool.name} {process.executable.name}when only the executable name is available;
- execute_tool {gen_ai.tool.name}otherwise.

The skill name SHOULD NOT be appended without the resource name.

Span kindSHOULD be INTERNAL.

Span statusSHOULD follow the [Recording Errors](https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/v1.44.0/docs/general/recording-errors.md)document.

Requirement level: [Recommended](https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/v1.44.0/docs/general/signal-requirement-level.md).

